.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Schnyder, Ryu, Furusaki, and Ludwig, and independently Kitaev, showed that every noninteracting Bloch or Bogoliubov-de Gennes Hamiltonian falls into one of just ten symmetry classes, fixed by whether time-reversal and particle-hole symmetry are present, the sign each squares to, and whether their product enforces a chiral symmetry -- and that the allowed topological invariant (\mathbb{Z}, \mathbb{Z}_2, or none) in a given spatial dimension depends only on which of the ten classes a Hamiltonian belongs to. Three of this package&#x27;s own topological models, already built for their own separate breakthroughs, are three different rows of that table:">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/condensed/topology/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_tenfold_way_classification_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/topology/plot_tenfold_way_classification`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Tenfold Way: Three Topological Invariants, One Classification Scheme</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/topology/plot_tenfold_way_classification`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Kane and Mele showed that adding intrinsic spin-orbit coupling to graphene -- two time-reversed copies of Haldane&#x27;s model, one per spin -- produces a time-reversal-symmetric insulator with a new, \mathbb{Z}_2-valued topological invariant protecting helical, counter-propagating edge states: the quantum spin Hall effect. Bernevig, Hughes, and Zhang then predicted the same physics in HgTe/CdTe quantum wells (the BHZ model), later observed experimentally -- the first realized topological insulator. kane_mele_hamiltonian and bhz_hamiltonian provide both microscopic realizations, and z2_invariant extracts the \mathbb{Z}_2 invariant from each via the spin-Chern-number reduction valid whenever s_z is conserved.">

.. only:: html

